            <div xml:id="d613">

                <pb facs="0640" n="528" xml:id="pg528"/>

                <note rend="inline" type="source">File No. 24607/11.</note>
                <head><hi rendition="#italic">The British Ambassador to the Secretary of
                    State.</hi></head>
                <opener><dateline rendition="#float-right"><placeName><hi rendition="#small-caps"
                                >British Embassy</hi>,<lb/><hi rendition="#italic"
                            >Washington</hi></placeName>, <date calendar="gregorian"
                            when="1910-05-11"><hi rendition="#italic">May 11,
                        1910</hi></date>.</dateline>
                    <seg rendition="#float-left">No. 77.]</seg></opener>
                <p><hi rendition="#small-caps">Sir</hi>: With reference to my note No. 75 of the 7th
                    instant, I have the honor to inform you that I have received a telegram from His
                    Majesty’s principal secretary of state for foreign affairs informing me that the
                    funeral of His late Majesty King Edward VII will take place at Windsor on the
                    20th instant.</p>
                <p>I have, etc.,</p>
                <closer>(For the Ambassador.)<lb/><signed><hi rendition="#small-caps">C. Innes
                            Mitchell.</hi></signed></closer>
            </div>
        </body>
    </text>
